  {
   "key": "0x03",
   "name": "character map select",
   "aliases": [
    "character map select register"
   ],
   "regions": [
    {
     "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
     "lines": "2931-3014"
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_seq.cpp",
     "function": "write_p3c5",
     "case": [
      "3"
     ]
    },
    {
     "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_seq.cpp",
     "function": "read_p3c5",
     "case": [
      "3"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "rows": [
    {
     "n": "1",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "The Character Map Select register, index 03 at hex 03C5: in alphanumeric modes attribute bit 3 normally sets intensity, and can be redefined to switch character sets for 512 characters.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2931-2936",
       "sha": "bceb165c050c7c074b869c93ce9fa0bffa3240a6495d6985710d69bb8bb667d1"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "2",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "To enable it, set the extended memory bit in the Memory Mode register and select different values for character maps A and B.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2937-2940",
       "sha": "24bdb0cf936d067c8d37deda3afcd1624fa6d3eff7d0b514098302493d863671"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "3",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "BIOS supports this function as a call within the character generator routines.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2941-2942",
       "sha": "84892976963340482f7bb88808b216b8b2e1011124831bcc7a84f1a47454db23"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "4",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "MAH (bit 5) and MBH (bit 4) are the most-significant selection bits for the locations of character maps A and B.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2956-2961",
       "sha": "0f8c84d1d0c8e683a5be72cd5a1793c6d2646d670f6c1e356c287d15ed135657"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "5",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "MAL (bits 3, 2) and MAH (bit 5) select map A, the font table in map 2 used when attribute bit 3 is 1.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2962-2967",
       "sha": "687d2cdd59429cd5582205a3b0da0d40149ca0b8235827652fc1caa1cfbac81a"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "6",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bits 5, 3 and 2 select maps 0-7 in the 1st, 3rd, 5th and 7th 8KB of map 2 for 000-011, and the 2nd, 4th, 6th and 8th for 100-111.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2968-2977",
       "sha": "f679658d431d99f9c63bf14f03f66daa3840714421f5d76425d603cc87f505c4"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2978-2987",
       "sha": "3bfef78a05ff38113829914b5d636d085b3eb3b44883ebc9158eacae3c8e9f7d"
      },
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2988-2997",
       "sha": "18f234a65b27836cef38f19b201557669de595996b42676d9c16a6b83f6ceed7"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "7",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "MBL (bits 1, 0) and MBH (bit 4) select map B, the font table in map 2 used when attribute bit 3 is 0.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "2998-3003",
       "sha": "49425538427d8deb09dba50185bc08e45a757cc48de571e297e8d71fb793510c"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "8",
     "on": "is",
     "of": "doc",
     "text": "Bits 4, 1 and 0 select among the same eight 8KB locations of map 2 for character map B.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "datasheet:PS2-Video-Subsystems.raw.txt",
       "lines": "3004-3013",
       "sha": "1da51a5d59ab85eaa7ae4520ba0851917787bc7d8bbb8dbd72e81c6ae1bc7b05"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "n": "101",
     "on": "write",
     "of": "dosbox-x",
     "vs": "extra",
     "text": "A write first renders the pending output when render-on-demand is on, then stores the byte.",
     "quotes": [
      {
       "ref": "dosbox-x:src/hardware/vga_seq.cpp",
       "lines": "191-192",
       "sha": "b6d3f92e98c6ebae137e592145a52ecdc08afb93c3f6186632af25282b855c91"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
